Qt 6.7.3 compiler compatibility corrections, adapted locally for Tidecoin.

Preserve Qt ordering representations while converting to the standard library,
complete types before SFINAE checks, and remove the QChar/QStringView include cycle.
Applied to target Qt and native Qt tools. Qt's original source licenses apply.

Based on Qt upstream work by Thiago Macieira, Giuseppe D'Angelo and
Allan Sandfeld Jensen (reviewed through Bitcoin PR 34754):
7fccc79dd5744ea837ffe200bbfc9f2756870220 (ordering representations)
3312e89b47f8c2ea0b4263b39841c25b83a37332 (regular expression completeness)
05f201a3d559452287b20becb960de3a50249540 (QChar range conversion)
679e8bda1eb0cc98acb981e9a10204bed1c179f2 (QBitArray completeness)
27230157212c32420e71b28870d6c77630c3dc37 (QAnyStringView assertions)
d68fc6ecc88a0e4532754b1a9f209881a248f4ee (QByteArrayView include)

